  {
    "sha": "dc740604d295bf8a69aeb374259321f82994d803",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVK7UKNoAKGRjNzQwNjA0ZDI5NWJmOGE2OWFlYjM3NDI1OTMyMWY4Mjk5NGQ4MDM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "u7-u7",
        "email": "116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T04:19:55Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T04:19:55Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(mysql): merge minute metrics under one row lock (#97)\n\nstore_metrics_minute() read the row, merged counters in Python, then wrote\nwith a separate SELECT + UPDATE/INSERT. Two instances flushing the same\nminute could both read the old value and overwrite each other, and a\nconcurrent insert could lose the whole batch to a duplicate-key error that\nthe outer except swallowed.\n\nRun the read-merge-write in one transaction with SELECT ... FOR UPDATE and\nretry once on a duplicate key or deadlock. Add unit regressions for the\ninsert and merge paths.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "f2872f02b7576f6eb00f3e3f7623919b502a5395",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/trees/f2872f02b7576f6eb00f3e3f7623919b502a5395"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/commits/dc740604d295bf8a69aeb374259321f82994d803",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2D1rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs+MQAFpDgRyGcVJfdhVHRZnA/h0j\nuxjnZ4b5D2Cz2PNlQzXb3ADUb4/AnU2ndcki9stTqs3avLnasDQkY7/UnKIzlB4D\nYN0liXm2+j5sv4U5NtXDZzcILxU0uS+tP+kuymoYTMlyBneAvZwz+FJOL3zDrSUw\ngcZEaU0rqYAb33fPfkSOREEs18Xg+b7uPB5gn3HIK1NY4Wk4SU03NLlRdUSQh940\nvTTj3fcTOYBYv+6t+cfvdPHjxmAyL8ORvHSlmKpv/h6Ri3+g9906oeyylXBXUoIa\nMOSHaB0gsxHtFRqelfpGoI+tya3nOfJrI+acUU7Ro2AX8niJOH9CfuHr6zdScKY5\neM+8D8LwoEf2o9xoVFyXMWw17r6bJSY0Df2j6PHwGs5iwtwESj4O61UVBZ3SRx6u\nxmCJJ38LjbFdBC5fppFdZCOoZRFKcQ0D/JyQ4w+TSLQpxgcVjZDbWNjJ0XXVKlXn\nOdHViu2EKQsimvAl3V+62sHnkm85HJs/XFt+ReATDo99i08ywzlYRcw7gJsVg6a2\nxe8F1yF9NEC7rwF04ehlrCt6vXUEsdrE1jTOkhbqAopCUpAC9mQP4TJFrqj/2W1W\na59cqOeel4eKEkHZOvGMDH1QGWHC0ap1K6RJe+51GiGUybaEB32uFtvGoeTmqeF0\nb8bd+pCYDNlrDdz5LPN0\n=E0zd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree f2872f02b7576f6eb00f3e3f7623919b502a5395\nparent 55bf946bccef289f80a20aa9c0b0c6a0fdbe7fb3\nauthor u7-u7 <116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com> 1792556395 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792556395 +0800\n\nfix(mysql): merge minute metrics under one row lock (#97)\n\nstore_metrics_minute() read the row, merged counters in Python, then wrote\nwith a separate SELECT + UPDATE/INSERT. Two instances flushing the same\nminute could both read the old value and overwrite each other, and a\nconcurrent insert could lose the whole batch to a duplicate-key error that\nthe outer except swallowed.\n\nRun the read-merge-write in one transaction with SELECT ... FOR UPDATE and\nretry once on a duplicate key or deadlock. Add unit regressions for the\ninsert and merge paths.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "verified_at": "2026-10-21T04:19:56Z"
      }
