  },
  {
    "sha": "3370a715dd5c76d70bd52b34a21185bbf4e5d21c",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVK7UKNoAKDMzNzBhNzE1ZGQ1Yzc2ZDcwYmQ1MmIzNGEyMTE4NWJiZjRlNWQyMWM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "u7-u7",
        "email": "116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T04:19:38Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T04:19:38Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(client): stop both owned event loops on close (#91)\n\nA solo client creates a write loop and a separate search loop, but close()\nstopped only the write loop and __aexit__ stopped neither. Every client\ninstance against a long-lived process therefore leaked the search thread,\nits selector and its 50ms self-wakeup timer. _LoopThread.stop() also left\nthe loop object unclosed.\n\nStop every owned loop from one idempotent helper used by both close() and\n__aexit__, leave shared-runtime loops to the runtime, and close the loop\nafter its thread exits. Add lifecycle regressions for both modes.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "8086eb27413143ce7b73136c1a70f7e5058ece31",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/trees/8086eb27413143ce7b73136c1a70f7e5058ece31"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/commits/3370a715dd5c76d70bd52b34a21185bbf4e5d21c",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2D1aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3swQAIgoLdegYk6+gPzcWsZiZC7o\n89+HK9M85pZHx6vehDoCTk7WWdIYwsOSnZyqCYBsxa317HdMDDU+hvguxraJMh08\nCBNz/xe/y0u7eydJ5ven9Fxoudg/v0JYhU3PYPM3D2vuTF8XgnOPBf0UKjgeRycq\nOxgK/gNv5PPCRwKZYKADFwZY9YL6F0kZmBc30pUf6HP80STa4cSeDxCfR/wsKIUA\n3G/wkHnHBGgjFpjvHeXefUrKz+29WuRp2Prw2XiHEdEKQdeekpP3H+qFAVicv+b9\n63uUh8u9bbS1O84cYza6cV9AqhhO6hN6t4sNKpownRj2NLi4V6+Qb93AUt/nvfZ0\noLxCTzW5ehzBxO9hrEDU5pmdCbStMo5jyalJDg+h2nqitEOZRfWqUuJb1JKTMIwH\nho8T3PZiRP357mNHvnQrtUDimtAcNteH7ZtoifVStfKNd+vaq+pyBqpjhN3S2BH6\nrde1rhPz9rct6lbjtkHHpP0ym2VaW75AN7jO1+DZ+dga0tOGcOK6OXe4xttEj69K\nbrYvevwpxAUC31aBp70Z/6veK3V3hREjXxvpwyGJ2ZU/+sv5B/yGm6Osko+uKLm/\ndjU0SIqZvuFq1/UBcIqPETYuGQri077c2lacmQNMGDALd53KjpExQd+OA4FkcQ94\n0Wh79yGbUHIti+uoi6w0\n=dht9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 8086eb27413143ce7b73136c1a70f7e5058ece31\nparent 638d1b7bde428ae8641f229eae374bbe9e9aa5a9\nauthor u7-u7 <116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com> 1792556378 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792556378 +0800\n\nfix(client): stop both owned event loops on close (#91)\n\nA solo client creates a write loop and a separate search loop, but close()\nstopped only the write loop and __aexit__ stopped neither. Every client\ninstance against a long-lived process therefore leaked the search thread,\nits selector and its 50ms self-wakeup timer. _LoopThread.stop() also left\nthe loop object unclosed.\n\nStop every owned loop from one idempotent helper used by both close() and\n__aexit__, leave shared-runtime loops to the runtime, and close the loop\nafter its thread exits. Add lifecycle regressions for both modes.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "verified_at": "2026-10-21T04:19:39Z"
      }
    },
