  },
  {
    "sha": "d6890793ec336367a5825d47279868b8c19aea67",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVK7UKNoAKGQ2ODkwNzkzZWMzMzYzNjdhNTgyNWQ0NzI3OTg2OGI4YzE5YWVhNjc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "u7-u7",
        "email": "116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T04:19:28Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T04:19:28Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sdk): repair FAISS embedding lookup, dedup pairing, and episode summaries (#84)\n\n* fix(faiss): reconstruct embeddings for dedup and episode summaries\n\nNormal upsert paths store only the payload and the FAISS index position.\nget_embeddings() looked for an \"embedding\" key that only update_payload\never wrote, so it returned an empty mapping for every upserted node. Search\ndedup and episode summaries therefore saw no vectors on the FAISS backend.\n\nReconstruct the vector from the live index position, guarded by the same\n_idx_to_id check search() uses, and keep the stored fallback for nodes\nupdated through update_payload. Add a regression test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(search): pair dedup markers with their source search result\n\nThe public items are filtered by the requested layers, but the private\ndedup view was built with zip(result.memories, public_items). Once one\nresult is filtered out every later _memory_kind shifts by one, so a\ncanonical_state can enter fuzzy dedup and be shadowed, or an ordinary fact\ncan silently skip dedup.\n\nBuild both views in the same loop, from the same source element, and add a\nregression test for the filtered case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(episode): use the writer's vector store for background summaries\n\n_schedule_episode_summary accessed self.vector_store, which MemoryWriter\nnever defines. The AttributeError was swallowed by the task's except block,\nso every closed episode silently skipped its L3 summary.\n\nResolve the store through the existing async _get_vector_store() accessor\nand cover the scheduled task with a regression test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "f419a3404fc62013bc2968232e824932be7feecb",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/trees/f419a3404fc62013bc2968232e824932be7feecb"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/commits/d6890793ec336367a5825d47279868b8c19aea67",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2D1QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjHgQACslobJwP5TwJi80vL75Zyrj\nYG3L+w77ShPd9jStZI30MtuU6qKMmpXIsNTUSiwmvFt+sK/pRU8UGBLRfHAAzh1Z\nwv0l5bOCJ5oHD4pRe8PA37okPZ3+4qz2E7lEfgZiGJtySNxUJNzyKdRJthFwIJw4\nd2wkKmboe+TgfjEDa7R4lUPNeSjQVwCoG82woS15e+6WPv98GioSWVUvcU20lWJ1\nbMO12bPmQdz46P+1xnTBivd077AqF7kn+Q8cP70WXVBH02tRaQvoMwWZobVTXbFS\nbxhkftw3EVy1JVg0rnKh2Ikl1UJKNRodDfzkSCcXW1199gOTFEUiqTZfv4ZKP4QQ\nUOusj1r2iDTu49BK8GBlscKRFz2RbaogNcsWnAH54oR/atQyKVjV/1CDqAg/drf5\n2gAW965MmDK0moD7bHmwgYm98ZdBf8BtTxUmGi/LJsUHH6VvwQ/B0W1GOWg30hq/\njEN3Cu8PdhPjw1/K9UFP0OHfB/jel3poPKm7+MOL92WYupLAdfxQXmzSIDNLuZM2\nW8YHX5inGfIG+G9GKsqsPF4ZHLd/fhmQXw9hDdlF6adKl1OjRs0WZ9WaDWw8ahWZ\nJdUdqJ7fxni3qsRRpHh6+svZ9CFYcjTGChvEU9zWLTZKuXgCrTKE5eEybM89/3gV\n38bW6qYsFtewvH+B89qU\n=Gp2L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree f419a3404fc62013bc2968232e824932be7feecb\nparent 32bf05f821d371fa1dc67c39930cd3f21783f4ee\nauthor u7-u7 <116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com> 1792556368 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792556368 +0800\n\nfix(sdk): repair FAISS embedding lookup, dedup pairing, and episode summaries (#84)\n\n* fix(faiss): reconstruct embeddings for dedup and episode summaries\n\nNormal upsert paths store only the payload and the FAISS index position.\nget_embeddings() looked for an \"embedding\" key that only update_payload\never wrote, so it returned an empty mapping for every upserted node. Search\ndedup and episode summaries therefore saw no vectors on the FAISS backend.\n\nReconstruct the vector from the live index position, guarded by the same\n_idx_to_id check search() uses, and keep the stored fallback for nodes\nupdated through update_payload. Add a regression test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(search): pair dedup markers with their source search result\n\nThe public items are filtered by the requested layers, but the private\ndedup view was built with zip(result.memories, public_items). Once one\nresult is filtered out every later _memory_kind shifts by one, so a\ncanonical_state can enter fuzzy dedup and be shadowed, or an ordinary fact\ncan silently skip dedup.\n\nBuild both views in the same loop, from the same source element, and add a\nregression test for the filtered case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(episode): use the writer's vector store for background summaries\n\n_schedule_episode_summary accessed self.vector_store, which MemoryWriter\nnever defines. The AttributeError was swallowed by the task's except block,\nso every closed episode silently skipped its L3 summary.\n\nResolve the store through the existing async _get_vector_store() accessor\nand cover the scheduled task with a regression test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "verified_at": "2026-10-21T04:19:28Z"
      }
