  {
    "sha": "4e44f59026726ad89f8bbda347d7604ad0971aa6",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVK7UKNoAKDRlNDRmNTkwMjY3MjZhZDg5ZjhiYmRhMzQ3ZDc2MDRhZDA5NzFhYTY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "u7-u7",
        "email": "116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T04:19:14Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T04:19:14Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(import): report oversized source files as file_too_large (#108)\n\nThe access gate refuses a file over the per-root max_file_bytes with\nFILE_TOO_LARGE, but both discovery_failure_code() and _scan_failure_code()\ncollapsed everything except budget and symlink failures into\nUNSUPPORTED_SCHEMA. A user with a 3 GiB Codex rollout therefore saw\n\"unsupported schema\" while the parser was fine; the only problem was size.\n\nMap the access gate's FILE_TOO_LARGE onto the existing ScanIssueCode.\nFILE_TOO_LARGE on both paths, and update the enum comment to say it covers\nboth the import's per-file ceiling and the access gate.\n\nThe per-file limit itself is unchanged.\n\nFixes #102.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "1ace02464f1295ad83317dd23e473c55ca843087",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/trees/1ace02464f1295ad83317dd23e473c55ca843087"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/commits/4e44f59026726ad89f8bbda347d7604ad0971aa6",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2D1CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX2AQACntTUom3hoOvU/gT3eZGQJR\nHFICjDCdI/0CIAYA1oT6b1uNkRNtEuewHQr3AO6R8qXF9LJB6zxE5zrOF2hlnLVd\niM19hW/Y1itv0kwZbAxvMLIg4MYf1yQFfk98ke38DLYMQYpsqiAVwtIv0gzh+tdS\nCYRVJPozYYCmLB5zwWHlIPJnzTIySvhgqdfmrUBhWYKkZ2RxINIj8pc91pwXL5Cl\nGU776/XDVg6ciDVDFmIkpJVhbMBs/I4V2cqbFBGAaId/7NGRIMEnGZPMInm+Ka0N\n3x5mkpG1s9uYhZ3g/EihjSlqmKsWoRPx5ltHONGf8BWmU0Iayt6eCQN6x/BcBCkd\nVKvTVU/XX8S33GHzQSPLm9mep281YlfnPEPfLmVnKPXM0LSxvxsqLohItAds0q24\nHUrpKx3YhVC3h5rDkDNUlsglQ6jB7xKZS49zA8YL25AXm3HViV9ucaB0tHCp6Nq3\nz/TF99eMfcVIlxS/trUw9hxi8Aqh2E0G05HW5JRtF7ZvL1+WYf9he8YGd3jtL2zC\nEuG41azOohfvFMeqM7pk2EYxUcDNH+s9qoFCoRVS7oGiE9TeTlpBTP0eLAZlVZtp\nXKCKUKPdSfam7nesjc4ULeq6w4g/F0wUFbn9D+Fe0qHXvUFZaPepYdF8Rr/M8hM5\nBGyYSG2ivke1orCHNr53\n=PI5t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 1ace02464f1295ad83317dd23e473c55ca843087\nparent 35bd56ddd09d29b924ef33a84850d8883eaf1e39\nauthor u7-u7 <116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com> 1792556354 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792556354 +0800\n\nfix(import): report oversized source files as file_too_large (#108)\n\nThe access gate refuses a file over the per-root max_file_bytes with\nFILE_TOO_LARGE, but both discovery_failure_code() and _scan_failure_code()\ncollapsed everything except budget and symlink failures into\nUNSUPPORTED_SCHEMA. A user with a 3 GiB Codex rollout therefore saw\n\"unsupported schema\" while the parser was fine; the only problem was size.\n\nMap the access gate's FILE_TOO_LARGE onto the existing ScanIssueCode.\nFILE_TOO_LARGE on both paths, and update the enum comment to say it covers\nboth the import's per-file ceiling and the access gate.\n\nThe per-file limit itself is unchanged.\n\nFixes #102.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>",
        "verified_at": "2026-10-21T04:19:14Z"
      }
