  },
  {
    "sha": "35bd56ddd09d29b924ef33a84850d8883eaf1e39",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVK7UKNoAKDM1YmQ1NmRkZDA5ZDI5YjkyNGVmMzNhODQ4NTBkODg4M2VhZjFlMzk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "u7-u7",
        "email": "116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T04:19:10Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T04:19:10Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(runtime): start the reader when the supervisor owns the Core (#99)\n\nreaderEnabled was only honored on the attach path. The normal first launch\nspawns its own Core and returned from start() without calling startReader(),\nso the read-only Reader never ran: no reader_port in the receipt and every\nread fell back to Core.\n\nStart the Reader after every successful owned start (first launch, race\nrecovery and relaunch). Clear readerChild when it exits so a later restart\ncan spawn a fresh one, and stop the old Reader before a relaunch. Add a\npublic-start regression using fake child processes.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "dc4241aedab927d2943005b9551208ebe4354579",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/trees/dc4241aedab927d2943005b9551208ebe4354579"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/commits/35bd56ddd09d29b924ef33a84850d8883eaf1e39",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2D0+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbGUQAK5eJjnwxzSogeQPVs/f19/q\nDRWWCm5Bux7g5awGNf6IHuDLUkuPhYAKOOXhd57quckbN9MvPtkXTtENqWljOHAj\nkIbB7HrC3fJHgGTLHVHma9pu5Vo1mwnQkoizpAkjEhMx6jJvXRuoQiRpMpqIRQNE\nQtU/bVH8vBK6lhmnIUWdqxXzqqbiS2n0cbglLWy/dZnrGTChLySabixuv0f3TX7m\n2E/NbUojXzlTsvx3P391gdiM9kUaXloyU1WQ3hdBFIcllswo5iPn7XeKD3sNzY+g\ngbB6qxL5cffVJLouHkVLoBhNnx07uGNKvBD/g+Stx4nl5PBdGIiaBngkgyjqwyM6\nzbthckLhcn00F9CH2dGAHhDxx8ezTk6cHTnwP7uaVz/Tvrw5QmYV/ChbWWsMHb8A\n7RtcKe8baijJG/0+5IbrJCGMRoysvl8+u5sNkgE4CDl7FcM02ywcwVQascT4gx0b\nTSj8Qj103QtiOs7mNipwKsfYmtCCK+3r8oG+eLSTvalEUzRdhiSDhJCAYmRleAoY\nAmRRG/3mAqns9mqTO7V891LcIzXAPECEQ854Ay19D8bvPD9FY/cgMYo7623I4vjD\nuQhOQN9qY3NQDrie+PNZrmm7xkrvrvFcKmIPczEVPy7GH5clS7bRFTDhLXXVDJy5\nPQPos0+3DHu2BaMzUEJ1\n=7F+M\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree dc4241aedab927d2943005b9551208ebe4354579\nparent 2cea39da4f9f536e81122bda0ec299e0fd5bc0e7\nauthor u7-u7 <116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com> 1792556350 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792556350 +0800\n\nfix(runtime): start the reader when the supervisor owns the Core (#99)\n\nreaderEnabled was only honored on the attach path. The normal first launch\nspawns its own Core and returned from start() without calling startReader(),\nso the read-only Reader never ran: no reader_port in the receipt and every\nread fell back to Core.\n\nStart the Reader after every successful owned start (first launch, race\nrecovery and relaunch). Clear readerChild when it exits so a later restart\ncan spawn a fresh one, and stop the old Reader before a relaunch. Add a\npublic-start regression using fake child processes.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "verified_at": "2026-10-21T04:19:10Z"
      }
    },
