  {
    "sha": "059e3a49037d45d03cfaddb6a8e78b5d8d5179ff",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVK7UKNoAKDA1OWUzYTQ5MDM3ZDQ1ZDAzY2ZhZGRiNmE4ZTc4YjVkOGQ1MTc5ZmY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "VE5PER-17",
        "email": "miaoranstudio@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T03:40:28Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T03:40:28Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(runtime): accept profile-scoped host ids in the host permission layer (#70)\n\n* fix(runtime): accept profile-scoped host ids in the host permission layer\n\nDeepSeek Harness configures recall per profile, so recall-hosts.ts reports\n`deepseek-harness:<profile>` as the host id. The CLI accepts that shape and\nprints it from `host list`, but the runtime rejected it twice:\n\n  - HostPermissions.supported() tested `[a-z][a-z0-9-]*`, so preview/install\n    answered host_permission_transport_unsupported for every Harness profile.\n  - HostGrantStore.validHostId() applied the same restriction, so even a\n    supported host could not create its installation or pass the load-time\n    revalidation.\n\nA host id is an opaque label: the installation directory is a digest of it,\nso a colon never becomes a path component. Both checks now allow one optional\n`:<profile>` segment, matching the CLI's existing HOST_ID.\n\nAdds an integration test that previews a real `cordis.patch.yml` install for\n`deepseek-harness:desktop` and a grant-store test that the colon survives a\nreload, plus a regression for malformed ids.\n\n* fix(runtime): share one host-id grammar across CLI, permissions and grants\n\nReview follow-up: the three layers had three different host-id rules, so the\nCLI could list an id the permission layer (or the grant store) then refused.\nThey now import `isHostId` from `@one-memory/contracts`, which is the only\ndefinition:\n\n  - host: 1..64 chars, alphanumeric first, lower-case letters/digits/hyphens\n  - optional `:<profile>`: 1..32 chars, alphanumeric first\n  - total <= 97, and the pattern asserts true end-of-input so a trailing\n    newline cannot pass\n\nDigit-leading ids stay accepted (the CLI always took them), and the profile\nsegment is the only colon allowed. Boundary cases live in\n`packages/contracts/src/host-id.test.ts`; the grant-store and permission tests\ncover the same grammar from their side.\n\nPackaging: contracts is a source-only workspace package, so every bundle that\nnow imports it for a value inlines it (`noExternal`): host-bridge entries,\nthe built Claude Code hook assets, and the CLI. Without that the emitted CJS\nasks Node for a `.js` file that only exists as `.ts` and the MCP entry fails\nat startup.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Vesper <226942762+VE5PER-17@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Vesper <hb.ran@foxmail.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "790265d1c148979eeb1be84e6ffa1883ab7e4cc0",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/trees/790265d1c148979eeb1be84e6ffa1883ab7e4cc0"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/commits/059e3a49037d45d03cfaddb6a8e78b5d8d5179ff",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2DQsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ4QQAIFnWDqx1RdFzvnEPr4KK7my\nY8x5VHFeq5UJ0Nb3L0V/arMbQ5LFNXm8LlWyrOrVZM0pPgcY8Wtdcw1E3QKNkdkx\nQmjU8AMemXWUEOtLoyIiL2nmXd76IhKV+Rk/++Ifwa+Pw3noresoMgLF5T3etSeL\nEUKkNDkFx0c81HCRVm5Dyo3qKzY0Yu1m8WXInyP2HaqYcemqSKKy53+Q2LkQ9pQs\nu0ZVqkn02BwuSvNlMVUd91EHJLCiZqFNg8L1QJJ9OuQNYeWLS234E2guyjcX5z0Z\nmtcKmuOE+zPuuA3ELzJ8G8pk8gvuyyps5IlW9ogi2oLinjQiXH6ZV6oIbv1nJ/r5\nvrgLeY/TYbdrw6D+XQxyfILSO4obf9/n/F/egD2SdSKPOjNGOkmREtPWHeL6psII\nLojwWxZ6VmmSX/COMnGfW3mt+vO/AneV+Y2oZJMrOUeobungYm+WEDtwyCxFzc1o\n8Hm5DuhMYAO0C0zxjj/BrIZ3mjmYYLx1JCKKBOUalTrYo5ufXR7B4TdvJbsWHQ1Z\nrcZ+VdTqkGG3EgMxi20Dic2g9iv6pGwVtVmWsLcIkABU+CckUiRO4FufUtf6gm2x\nmj1/KjLX1hQ+GF1SDu2Xxnw1RGNeJBk5efgqfMAebKwPh0Po4ds0zpWnGp8UB5Q0\nuQGn+tJpa7wSAlyV1gRA\n=rrjv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 790265d1c148979eeb1be84e6ffa1883ab7e4cc0\nparent 0a9b10dbfc1371ed667de1cd760b736fe4bb1499\nauthor VE5PER-17 <miaoranstudio@gmail.com> 1792554028 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792554028 +0800\n\nfix(runtime): accept profile-scoped host ids in the host permission layer (#70)\n\n* fix(runtime): accept profile-scoped host ids in the host permission layer\n\nDeepSeek Harness configures recall per profile, so recall-hosts.ts reports\n`deepseek-harness:<profile>` as the host id. The CLI accepts that shape and\nprints it from `host list`, but the runtime rejected it twice:\n\n  - HostPermissions.supported() tested `[a-z][a-z0-9-]*`, so preview/install\n    answered host_permission_transport_unsupported for every Harness profile.\n  - HostGrantStore.validHostId() applied the same restriction, so even a\n    supported host could not create its installation or pass the load-time\n    revalidation.\n\nA host id is an opaque label: the installation directory is a digest of it,\nso a colon never becomes a path component. Both checks now allow one optional\n`:<profile>` segment, matching the CLI's existing HOST_ID.\n\nAdds an integration test that previews a real `cordis.patch.yml` install for\n`deepseek-harness:desktop` and a grant-store test that the colon survives a\nreload, plus a regression for malformed ids.\n\n* fix(runtime): share one host-id grammar across CLI, permissions and grants\n\nReview follow-up: the three layers had three different host-id rules, so the\nCLI could list an id the permission layer (or the grant store) then refused.\nThey now import `isHostId` from `@one-memory/contracts`, which is the only\ndefinition:\n\n  - host: 1..64 chars, alphanumeric first, lower-case letters/digits/hyphens\n  - optional `:<profile>`: 1..32 chars, alphanumeric first\n  - total <= 97, and the pattern asserts true end-of-input so a trailing\n    newline cannot pass\n\nDigit-leading ids stay accepted (the CLI always took them), and the profile\nsegment is the only colon allowed. Boundary cases live in\n`packages/contracts/src/host-id.test.ts`; the grant-store and permission tests\ncover the same grammar from their side.\n\nPackaging: contracts is a source-only workspace package, so every bundle that\nnow imports it for a value inlines it (`noExternal`): host-bridge entries,\nthe built Claude Code hook assets, and the CLI. Without that the emitted CJS\nasks Node for a `.js` file that only exists as `.ts` and the MCP entry fails\nat startup.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Vesper <226942762+VE5PER-17@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Vesper <hb.ran@foxmail.com>",
        "verified_at": "2026-10-21T03:40:29Z"
      }
