  {
    "sha": "0a9b10dbfc1371ed667de1cd760b736fe4bb1499",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVK7UKNoAKDBhOWIxMGRiZmMxMzcxZWQ2NjdkZTFjZDc2MGI3MzZmZTRiYjE0OTk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "u7-u7",
        "email": "116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T03:40:23Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T03:40:23Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(auth): require the local token on reader internal endpoints (#82)\n\nThe /internal/semantic-ids, /internal/call-event and\n/internal/graph-snapshot routes were registered directly on the app without\nthe local_api_guard dependency used by every other route. Any local process\ncould read memory graph content, probe semantic IDs, or forge call events\nwithout authorization.\n\nMount the same guard on all three routes. The Reader already sends\nAuthorization: Bearer <core_api_token>, so its calls keep working. Add\nregression tests for both the 401 and authorized paths.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "451a638e41bdd0affe3e25a0cf35830921a9b2d8",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/trees/451a638e41bdd0affe3e25a0cf35830921a9b2d8"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/commits/0a9b10dbfc1371ed667de1cd760b736fe4bb1499",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2DQnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhnYQAKo4mFGwncT2RQwjpcP8gPxj\nWvvqS8WHUYVoUy1CGEmGpryvTHepjm/TapyYMcnnBlZrLRBUMHGBYsozzX/edOOC\nigbr6Ih1N1Cis+ZK1Ql0Yduz+PdCBP/5gJAreE3tBWPJPALFj53KxTOnbNuojq3l\n3nU8JC0RPdJYveD/fBluxs1OY8eTMADdCj8sQz7+whz5iEK5kIqj0HpRWLP+icXn\ndqCi2ggwV4PZ/YUax2tNJZ+6SQfQgmSAfPlBmC5/cz2PFFn6kD1grJC+1U6EYh76\n54C8hT8nw3bQp3M21m3eEyTm4uUmCqb9umO1NDPSwxMhzq8k2fsedBB1FQVdEWV+\nomtqZSRYyzhJxM4lNDAGolus54P4iNk31q4BrZNO8pO1esJ4rEPFfm3hJA2Ksynd\nG8BSvmdoIl6hgQu/doO2GJ0vb+eteYgPztM6EjZC/2QVFZEjozmzDW/N5OKYhySk\nzd3Y9reLzCK/QsjO30ckFMlsuFsr44sMdZesizxFLo3bdCDrbjYGPwYGd7r14azb\nzgokvF09VAOeFqe8kS7in0HWJqSYqiJl6j9ZOY84yIwV8b5hV0LCTXeuLMfbU0wE\n9VYwu13dZMHXC75pWjeOttU3puf/RhM2+EI5/yHqqr/22SU/3spgvRorfr53gDAI\n+xie51ipt7PUfm2VT1Cl\n=Fygv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 451a638e41bdd0affe3e25a0cf35830921a9b2d8\nparent 3a74a334564a0c1a866c899ca881ede1f8a556a0\nauthor u7-u7 <116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com> 1792554023 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792554023 +0800\n\nfix(auth): require the local token on reader internal endpoints (#82)\n\nThe /internal/semantic-ids, /internal/call-event and\n/internal/graph-snapshot routes were registered directly on the app without\nthe local_api_guard dependency used by every other route. Any local process\ncould read memory graph content, probe semantic IDs, or forge call events\nwithout authorization.\n\nMount the same guard on all three routes. The Reader already sends\nAuthorization: Bearer <core_api_token>, so its calls keep working. Add\nregression tests for both the 401 and authorized paths.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "verified_at": "2026-10-21T03:40:23Z"
      }
