  },
  {
    "sha": "4bc918af7a0a65e7cd12ed410eb60ac6eee63c5c",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVK7UKNoAKDRiYzkxOGFmN2EwYTY1ZTdjZDEyZWQ0MTBlYjYwYWM2ZWVlNjNjNWM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "u7-u7",
        "email": "116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T03:02:52Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-21T03:02:52Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(coding): apply agent and session scope to coding retrieval (#87)\n\nThe public search API accepts agent_ids / session_ids, and the chat reader\napplies them, but the coding path dropped both before calling the store.\nA caller that relies on agent or session boundaries could therefore recall\nfacts and experiences written by another agent or session of the same user.\n\nAccept the id lists in the coding store, filter them with IN clauses and\nin the post-fetch checks, and forward them from _search_coding. Singular\nagent_id / session_id stay supported for existing callers. Add store-level\nand client-level regressions for the filtered scopes.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "fbdc63bee5a099b38ad98a66ff8dcd58b99044b8",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/trees/fbdc63bee5a099b38ad98a66ff8dcd58b99044b8"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Memory/git/commits/4bc918af7a0a65e7cd12ed410eb60ac6eee63c5c",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2CtcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH3AQAF3MU0aXSd4dYW3PcyU5Ln4h\n/QBGjblEByGhRWKf3cNC8SIA9oBDy9tBAfBY6jTP1YrmkjqEIGpVE7IN4fm800rI\nqkHVCZhFDFtdtm/Nyska3BOBw8hTsEO8fS+yEfws+YIHVj05X0k2t2apA5noQ5H3\nPnywc2lgkES2S4lpARW/0DiDHtjDyy0Uhxz+5tQj5LWR677ECLkZXlqEfAxJE+xI\nc1GxDwzgv15EnKe0s2hndtVZ5SQ1Tvu0jjMB6jGyyRg9aCLvBWVwjcw1ANoDlElx\nL1uu82VL+u6PTZuvBaIJ+XBXJHV5zgDKfyfIpNO2025yoGqAWzfFnohj4Hk+rk2F\nglc3aMZM1jY1lxfahl5PxAwH8mD8salvQBRqBpn3FZFNtGc9hTAyM19zrQiIm6c8\nqHY8XrLKEDKCF89ewaABeN50jjNPZS3fJFq6r2xVuBOLF5wXXhwURZKAbwIhDJSl\nMAxldE4AvN0tKYt8sSaqUoH8hUFGxg3jyZUp6dQ4Z+TO+RsaauLB39prq208r9Kz\nW6QrleiBx2EIkqOj4mr3Hy980ulmB8AHiHWG3sXi0wfxd5HSmVyY4XeogEZFwwaq\n3vHA1g5u0Ohm+J0EEEjTFDFsdq/jPiatmEbqn79Yyv7c9vVclKPhtCeAFTl66gPp\nuoS3AeY8UEQ0VW48ky/Y\n=o/eb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree fbdc63bee5a099b38ad98a66ff8dcd58b99044b8\nparent 75163a0d1ef3208fea932505d8d5e37296f16130\nauthor u7-u7 <116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com> 1792551772 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792551772 +0800\n\nfix(coding): apply agent and session scope to coding retrieval (#87)\n\nThe public search API accepts agent_ids / session_ids, and the chat reader\napplies them, but the coding path dropped both before calling the store.\nA caller that relies on agent or session boundaries could therefore recall\nfacts and experiences written by another agent or session of the same user.\n\nAccept the id lists in the coding store, filter them with IN clauses and\nin the post-fetch checks, and forward them from _search_coding. Singular\nagent_id / session_id stay supported for existing callers. Add store-level\nand client-level regressions for the filtered scopes.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "verified_at": "2026-10-21T03:02:52Z"
      }
    },
