        "payload": "tree 17fb49758a4b32a291e4f18463c92f8910fddb9f\nparent 8f1c4045e913566a6f40eb4451d68218b2307773\nauthor u7-u7 <116776533+u7-u7@users.noreply.github.com> 1792551749 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792551749 +0800\n\nfix(auth): validate loopback origins as IP addresses (#90)\n\nis_loopback_origin() accepted any hostname starting with \"127.\". That\nincludes ordinary DNS names such as 127.0.0.1.attacker.example, which an\nattacker can point at 127.0.0.1 and use for DNS rebinding against the\nlocal Core.\n\nKeep the exact loopback names and parse everything else with\nipaddress.ip_address(...).is_loopback. Add regressions for rebinding-style\nnames and IPv6 loopback.\n\nCo-authored-by: qiye.sjh <shijiahao_0802@youzan.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
